{"base_rate":0.3473541383989145,"brier":0.20183744911804613,"bss":0.10966861518970894,"bss_hi":0.230664833783518,"bss_lo":-0.04093648755899273,"chart":{"base":[512.4,72.0],"fp":[198.9,230.9],"lead":"62,222.1 272,193.3 482,164.6 692,126","note":{"base":"skill 0.11 — higher than 18% of cities","fp":"low end +0pp, high end +32pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 20% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 98% → rained 71%"},"rel":"62,462.4 152.5,429.2 470.9,374.3 680.4,161"},"country":"CN","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.21245590230664857,"ess":392.3216280925788,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Chongqing</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Chongqing rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>77%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 19.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.11, ranked 174 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(136&ndash;190) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>119</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>98</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>77%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Chongqing</b> <span class=\"muted\">China</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.11</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>136&ndash;190\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Chongqing &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Chongqing\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"