58,326.0 79.74571428571429,374.57142857142856 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"255.56309362279512\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"255.56309362279512\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,378.94117647058823 79.74571428571429,367.14285714285717 145.36538461538458,330.6666666666667 241.5465753424658,342.1095890410959 333.92602739726027,267.3150684931507 388.02239999999995,197.57333333333332 411.4233484162896,100.35294117647055\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 119 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"378.94117647058823\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 98 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"79.74571428571429\" cy=\"367.14285714285717\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"145.36538461538458\" cy=\"330.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 52%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"241.5465753424658\" cy=\"342.1095890410959\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"333.92602739726027\" cy=\"267.3150684931507\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 93%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"388.02239999999995\" cy=\"197.57333333333332\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 77% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 221 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.4233484162896\" cy=\"100.35294117647055\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(35%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Chongqing the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.23) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.12).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>-0.118</td><td class='num'>26.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>212</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.100</td><td class='num'>22.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>177</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.124</td><td class='num'>20.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>173</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.232</td><td class='num'>15.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":29.56026,"lon":106.55771,"n":737,"n_cities":213,"name":"Chongqing","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":119,"obs":0.008403361344537815,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.06142857142857142,"n":98,"obs":0.04081632653061224,"sig":false},{"hi":0.3640000000000003,"lo":0.16,"mean":0.24679487179487175,"n":78,"obs":0.14102564102564102,"sig":true},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.3640000000000003,"mean":0.5184931506849316,"n":73,"obs":0.1095890410958904,"sig":true},{"hi":0.87,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7794520547945205,"n":73,"obs":0.3150684931506849,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9720000000000004,"lo":0.87,"mean":0.9322666666666665,"n":75,"obs":0.5066666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9720000000000004,"mean":0.998371040723982,"n":221,"obs":0.7737556561085973,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":19.4,"provisional":false,"rank":174,"rank_hi":190.02499999999998,"rank_lo":136.0,"reliability":0.07273553100834622,"resolution":0.0983570277988647,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"chongqing","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Shanghai"}